# Generated by running the tests, not by anyone. Three of these were tracked, so a clean
# checkout could not run its own suite without producing a diff — which defeats any
# "working tree is clean after the build" assertion and invites `git commit -a` to sweep
# bytecode back in (slicr#15).
#
# They were also pinned to cpython-313 and pytest-8.4.1: wrong for any other interpreter,
# and regenerated rather than used by one.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# pytest and ruff caches — same argument, and both are already gitignored by habit
# everywhere else in the family.
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
